❯ /review security

Blocking

None.

Should fix

.claude/commands/review.md:4 — Bash(git diff:*) and Bash(git log:*) are prefix matches, so they also pre-approve flags that write files, such as git diff --output=<path>. The diff is untrusted data placed in the prompt, so injected text in it could make the model write to an arbitrary path without a permission prompt. The "Read-only" rule at line 26 is only a prompt instruction, not an enforced restriction. Fix: narrow the allowlist to the exact commands the template runs, e.g. Bash(git diff HEAD:*), Bash(git diff HEAD --stat), Bash(git log --oneline -10) and Bash(git status --short --branch). Alternatively, drop allowed-tools for the tools the model doesn't need, since the ! commands already run at expansion time.
.claude/commands/review.md:13 — git diff HEAD never includes untracked files. A new file such as a committed-by-mistake .env, a new route or a new test is invisible to the review until it is staged. Your first two /review runs returned "empty diff" while .claude/commands/ was untracked, which shows this. For a security review, this can hide the files most likely to contain secrets. Fix: add an untracked-files line to the context, e.g. - Untracked files: !git ls-files --others --exclude-standard``. Then either add Bash(git ls-files:*) to the allowlist or tell the reviewer to flag untracked files it cannot see.


Nits

.claude/commands/review.md:19 — $ARGUMENTS is interpolated raw into the prompt. This is fine for a local, user-invoked command, but the focus text is not delimited from the instructions. Wrapping it, e.g. Focus area: "$ARGUMENTS", would keep stray text from reading as an instruction.


Looks good

.claude/commands/review.md:5 — disable-model-invocation: true means only the user can trigger the review, so the model can't invoke it on its own.
.claude/commands/review.md:25 — it tells the reviewer to treat diff content as data, not instructions, which addresses prompt injection from reviewed code.
.claude/commands/review.md:27 — a secret found in the diff must be reported by file and line without reproducing its value, so the review output can't leak it.
.claude/commands/review.md:4 — allowed-tools is scoped to git read commands instead of a blanket Bash. It just needs tightening as described above.

